# Backend Python

## Structure

- `routers/` — HTTP endpoints; thin handlers, logic in `services/`
- `models/` — Pydantic schemas
- `db/` — persistence (sqlite_client legacy, domain_client relational)
- `transforms/` — one file per OSINT plugin via `@register`
- `connectors/` — PlatformConnector implementations
- `services/` — entity_resolution, audit, context_readiness
- `middleware/` — auth, rate_limit

## Conventions

- Type hints on all public functions
- `snake_case` functions/vars, `PascalCase` classes
- Use `logging` module — never `print()`; redact PII in log messages
- Async for I/O; `asyncio.to_thread` for sync OSINT libs

## Transform return contract

```python
{
  "nodes": [...],
  "edges": [...],
  "observations": [{
    "source": {"platform": str, "collection_method": str, "url": str|None},
    "content": dict,
    "confidence": float,
    "status": "UNVERIFIED|CONFIRMED|..."
  }],
  "log": ["sanitized step messages"]
}
```

## API

- Legacy: `/graph`, `/transforms`, `/workspaces`
- Domain: `/api/v1/dossiers`, `/api/v1/entities`, etc.
- Use proper HTTP status codes for new endpoints (404, 422, 429)

## Security

- Rate limit `/transforms/run`
- Validate enums for entity/relation types on v1 API
- Audit important mutations via `audit_events` table

## Tests

Add pytest in `backend/tests/` for new routers and services.
